# Normalise line endings, so a clone on another platform does not show every
# file as modified. Git stores LF and checks out whatever the platform wants.
#
# Added after a history rewrite left thirty files looking modified when their
# content was byte-identical: the working copy had LF and core.autocrlf wanted
# CRLF, which git reports as a difference but git diff does not show.
* text=auto
